---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Squiggle from '../components/Squiggle.astro';
import Picture from '../components/Picture.astro';
import { therapist, breadcrumb } from '../data/schema';
import WaveDivider from '../components/WaveDivider.astro';
import CTAButton from '../components/CTAButton.astro';
import { PARENT_SITE_URL } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Meet Your Therapist, Jo Wiseman | Charnwood Intimacy"
  description="Jo Wiseman is a BACP-registered psychotherapist training in psychosexual and relationship therapy with CICS, accredited by COSRT."
  path="/your-therapist/"
  schema={[therapist, breadcrumb([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Your Therapist', path: '/your-therapist/' },
  ])]}
>
  <section class="section section--white hero-section">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-photo">
        <Picture src="/images/jo-wiseman.jpg" alt="Jo Wiseman, Founder & Psychotherapist" width={700} height={875} loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Your Therapist</p>
        <h1>Jo Wiseman, Founder &amp; Psychotherapist</h1>
        <Squiggle />
        <p class="lead">
          Jo is a warm, curious and down-to-earth therapist offering a safe, non-judgemental
          space to explore whatever brings you here.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <WaveDivider from="var(--white)" to="var(--cream-alt)" />

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>About Jo</h2>
      <p>
        Jo Wiseman is the founder of Charnwood Counselling, a BACP-registered psychotherapist,
        and the therapist behind Charnwood Intimacy. She's currently completing the CICS Diploma
        in Psychosexual and Relationship Therapy, a two-year, COSRT and NCPS accredited programme
        delivered by the Contemporary Institute of Clinical Sexology (CICS), and is working
        towards full COSRT registration as a psychosexual and relationship therapist, the
        professional term for what many people search for as a sex therapist.
      </p>
      <p>
        Jo's approach is pluralistic and integrative: rather than fitting every client into one
        model, she draws on a range of therapeutic approaches to suit what each person needs,
        while keeping the client and the relationship at the centre of the work. Her training
        places a strong emphasis on gender, sexual, relationship and cultural diversity (GSRD),
        which means Charnwood Intimacy is a genuinely inclusive space for people of any gender,
        sexuality, relationship structure, culture or background.
      </p>
      <p>
        Jo understands that bringing sexual concerns to therapy takes real courage, and she
        brings the same warmth and respect to this work that clients already know from Charnwood
        Counselling.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <WaveDivider from="var(--cream-alt)" to="var(--white)" flip />

  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Training and Supervision</h2>
      <p>
        As part of her CICS Diploma, Jo is required to complete a minimum of 150 hours of
        supervised clinical practice, working with the full range of sexual and relationship
        presentations, alongside her own 50 hours of personal therapy over the course of the
        two-year programme. In practice, this means every piece of work Jo does is closely
        supervised by an experienced psychosexual therapist, and it's part of why introductory
        rates apply during this period (see <a href="/pricing-and-booking/">Pricing &amp; Booking</a>).
      </p>
      <p>
        This will be explained clearly to every new client before their first session, so there
        are no surprises, and so you can make an informed choice about starting therapy with Jo
        at this stage of her training.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <WaveDivider from="var(--white)" to="var(--cream-alt)" />

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Registrations</h2>
      <ul class="reg-list">
        <li>MBACP, British Association for Counselling and Psychotherapy</li>
        <li>Student member, College of Sexual and Relationship Therapists (COSRT)</li>
        <li>Studying towards the CICS Diploma in Psychosexual and Relationship Therapy</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">
        Registration status is reviewed regularly as Jo's training progresses. If you have any
        questions about her current status, she's very happy to talk it through with you before
        your first session.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <WaveDivider from="var(--cream-alt)" to="var(--teal-dark)" flip />

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Part of the Charnwood Counselling group</h2>
      <p>
        Charnwood Intimacy is part of the Charnwood Counselling group, based at The Old Arts
        College in Loughborough. If you're looking for general counselling, bereavement support
        or relationship counselling that isn't specifically sexual, visit
        {' '}
        <a href={PARENT_SITE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">charnwoodcounselling.co.uk</a>.
      </p>
      <CTAButton href="/pricing-and-booking/" variant="outline">Pricing &amp; Booking</CTAButton>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .hero-photo img {
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    max-width: 560px;
  }
  .prose > * {
    max-width: 800px;
  }
  .prose p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }
  .section--dark .prose p {
    color: var(--text-on-dark-soft);
  }
  .reg-list {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6em;
  }
  .note {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .hero-photo {
      max-width: 280px;
    }
  }
</style>
